From: qualixxe <qualixxe@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: set DSC range_max_qp[0]=8 for 10bpc/8bpp panels

VESA DSC 1.1 pre-SCR table sets rc_range_params[0].range_max_qp = 7 for
10 bpc @ 8 bpp, whereas Qualcomm's downstream SDM/SM7150 DSI driver and
Xiaomi's courbet K9A (36-02-0a) panel PPS override range_max_qp[0] to 8.
With 7, flat regions (such as solid console background rows) under-quantize
in range 0 and produce horizontal/right-edge DSC artifacts on K9A.

Override rc_range_params[0].range_max_qp to 8 in dsi_populate_dsc_params()
for 10 bpc / 8 bpp before computing RC parameters, keeping both the panel
PPS payload and DPU1 DSC_RANGE_MAX_QP_0 register in sync.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -1851,6 +1851,9 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	if (dsc->bits_per_component == 10 && drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc) == 8)
+		dsc->rc_range_params[0].range_max_qp = 8;
+
 	dsc->initial_scale_value = drm_dsc_initial_scale_value(dsc);
 	dsc->line_buf_depth = dsc->bits_per_component + 1;
 
